            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for that very one, then the Hindi for maybe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: माफ़ी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माफ़ी (māfī) — \"an apology, pardon\", the noun."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माफ़ी (māfī) चाहता हूँ — \"I beg your pardon\" (a woman says चाहती). It shares its root with माफ़ कीजिए."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माफ़ी (māfī) is usually traced, through Persian, to an Arabic word for \"pardon\" on the root ʿ-f-w, \"to pardon, excuse\" (Lane). It is the noun of the māf inside māf kījie, \"forgive me\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The apology as a thing you ask for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
