          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निमंत्रण (nimantraṇ) — \"an invitation\", the formal word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निमंत्रण (nimantraṇ) के लिए धन्यवाद — \"thank you for the invitation\", with के लिए and धन्यवाद."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A written invitation has the three parts of the short message you learned to write: the line that names the reader, प्रिय मीरा,; the sentences under it; and the writer's name at the foot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निमंत्रण (nimantraṇ) is Sanskrit nimantraṇa, \"invitation\", taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama. CDIAL lists its verb, nimantrayate, \"invites\", whose inherited forms survive as nyotnā, \"to invite\" (CDIAL 7235)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sorry, no problem, congratulations, wishes, and thanks for an invitation."
            }
          ]
        },
